-- title:
--   Exact rollout cost identity (Prop. 6.4.3)
-- statement:
--   **Proposition 6.4.3 (exact cost identity for the rollout algorithm).** For an **arbitrary** base heuristic $\mathcal{H}$ — sequentially improving or not — let $(i_1, \dots, i_{\bar m})$ be a path generated by a terminating run of the rollout algorithm from a non-destination node $i_1$ to a destination $i_{\bar m}$. Writing
--
--   $$\delta_i \;=\; \min_{j \in N(i)} H(j) \;-\; H(i)$$
--
--   for the defect at a node, the rollout cost decomposes exactly as
--
--   $$g(i_{\bar m}) \;=\; H(i_1) \;+\; \sum_{m=1}^{\bar m - 1} \delta_{i_m} .$$
--
--   The identity is a telescoping one: each rollout step realizes precisely the neighborhood minimum, so the improvements accumulate additively along the run. It immediately yields Prop. 6.4.2 — under sequential improvement every $\delta_i \le 0$, hence $g(i_{\bar m}) \le H(i_1)$ — but it says more, since it quantifies the improvement rather than merely bounding it, and it applies with no assumption on the heuristic at all. It is the discrete counterpart of the slack-accumulating bound of Prop. 6.3.2 for limited lookahead policies.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The defect takes the junk value $0$ at a node with no neighbors, which cannot occur along a run. The sum runs over the nodes of the path with the last one removed, in order and with multiplicity — a node visited twice contributes twice.
-- source:
--   D. P. Bertsekas, Dynamic Programming and Optimal Control, Vol. I, 3rd ed., Athena Scientific, 2005, Proposition 6.4.3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BertsekasGraphSearch

namespace BertsekasDP

theorem rollout_cost_decomposition {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]
    (G : BertsekasGraphSearch V) (H : BertsekasBaseHeuristic G)
    (l : List V) (hrun : BertsekasIsRolloutRun G H l)
    (i₁ : V) (hhead : l.head? = some i₁) (hstart : i₁ ∉ G.dest)
    (d : V) (hlast : l.getLast? = some d) :
    G.cost d = BertsekasHeurCost G H i₁ +
      (l.dropLast.map (BertsekasRolloutDelta G H)).sum := by sorry

end BertsekasDP
